Default project license: GPL-2.0-or-later (LICENSE).
Kernel, drivers and device trees: built as the OrchardLinux/orchard platform
layer (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard;
upstream snapshot at kernel/upstream.lock). A10/A7-A11 platform support
originates in HoolockLinux's Linux staging tree (GPL-2.0), integrated in
orchard's patches; the 16K page-size configuration is derived from
HoolockLinux/docs (GPL-2.0).
Pongo (pongo.bin) and m1n1 are OrchardLinux/orchard components; see
LICENSES/ in orchard (m1n1.txt, Pongo.txt, wireless-regdb.txt).
Apple/Broadcom/Z2 device firmware is never shipped: it is extracted from the
user's own iPadOS restore image at install time using orchard's public
firmware recipes (orchard/devices/j171/firmware.json, BSD-style recipe
metadata; recipe inputs/outputs only — no Apple firmware is redistributed).
Host CLI, install scripts and recovery runtime: OrchardLinux/orchard
(GPL-2.0-or-later).
Boot contract implementation, including m1n1 boot-manager patches: orchard
(GPL-2.0-or-later).
Resize APFS: MIT, https://github.com/OrchardLinux/resize-apfs
(Applies the disk-level "Adjust size" step; referenced, not redistributed).
Prior art credited: Project Sandcastle (Corellium,
https://github.com/corellium/projectsandcastle) and corellium/linux-sandcastle
(kernel: GPL-2.0; userspace utilities carry their own LICENSE files). No
Sandcastle source is redistributed; design lessons and the 16 KB ELF
alignment methodology are credited in docs/SANDCASTLE.md.
Android GSI binaries (Track A/B) are built from or referenced for testing:
AOSP (Apache-2.0) and LineageOS-derived community GSI builds (Apache-2.0);
see docs/RESEARCH.md for which builds are used and their licenses.
No Google GMS applications are included in default builds: default builds
are tracker-free and do not ship Google services.
Any other third-party component added later lists its license here, with the
checked upstream commit, before it is built into a release.
